def fibonacci(n):
    if n <= 1:
        return n
    a, b = 0, 1
    for _ in range(n - 1):
        a, b = b, a + b
    return b

This iterative function computes the nth Fibonacci number in O(n) time and O(1) space by maintaining only the two most recent values. It avoids the exponential overhead of naive recursion and the stack limits of recursive implementations.
